vkquake-ios overlay 0015: survive the 2026 rerelease's mismatched .md5anim
files (upstream Novum/vkQuake#980, Ironwail#550).

The 30th-anniversary update (2026-08-06) added Dawn of the Machine as the
`mg3` game dir. It ships progs/ogre_rocket.md5anim with a joint count that
disagrees with its sibling .md5mesh (39 vs 55), and the rocket ogre is
precached by nearly every map's entity list -- so `-game mg3 +map map1`
dies at load with "QUAKE ERROR: progs/ogre_rocket.md5anim has incorrect
joint count". The Sys_Error fires inside Mod_LoadMD5MeshModel, i.e. before
mod->extradata[PV_MD5] is assigned, and it fires regardless of
r_enhancedmodels because the MD5 is loaded and inspected either way.

Turn the fatal into a Con_Warning and unwind: MD5Anim_Load now returns a
qboolean, and the caller frees its allocations and returns with
extradata[PV_MD5] still NULL. Mod_Extradata_CheckSkin then sees exactly
one valid variant and returns the classic .mdl (which mg3 also ships for
this model), i.e. the same result as Models: classic -- but only for this
one model. Everything else in the episode keeps its enhanced mesh.

Measured over all 20 mg3 maps on the macOS oracle: every map spawns, and
progs/ogre_rocket is the ONLY model that warns.

UPSTREAM SUPERSESSION: this is a workaround for an upstream bug, not a
port feature. Novum/vkQuake#980 is open and assigned. DELETE this patch when a pin bump
brings upstream's own fix — see the checklist at the bottom of upstream.pin
for why "the build is still green" is not sufficient evidence to keep it.

